      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALMANZAS (2) switched from Bjorn Baker to Stirling Osland and returned from a five-month spell when a closing second over 1200m at Quirindi 24 days ago. Beaten just 1.6 lengths at Canterbury last prep which is outstanding form for a race of this calibre. Looks very hard to stop over the extra 200m today. WHISKEY AND WINE (1) has been runner-up at both appearances this prep, the latest over 1300m at Toowoomba where he did his best work late. Lightly raced four-year-old whose best is yet to come. HONNIBALL DRIVE (3) has only failed once in five career runs which was two back in town. Closed hard to finish a close fourth most recently over 1000m at Muswellbrook. This looks a most suitable assignment. RUFUS ATTICUS (9) made late inroads to clock in just behind the placegetters over 1250m at Gunnedah last start. Has had plenty of chances but is an each-way prospect. PINERO (8) needs a good track to show her best so today's conditions will suit.",
